y, Q in the quest,  \\nQ in the quick step, giving leadership a test.  \\nPolicy, people, and a podium glow\\u2014  \\nKeeping the nation moving wherever winds blow.\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:letter_frequency\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-202/memory/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-2265"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:6b801022bb8fe611ba58fcd3d038f8c6bfa28365271d814e015dd282501ba400", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2871", "family": "ifeval-source-2871", "sample_id": "sha256:2f3a1fc504e3b4489a91ba21c694bf7efa6f006a4414af97637574ed97abac77", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a poem about the history of reductions in the context of the church. Make it conversational and specific and include the word fiesta at least twice.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"In the old Guaran\\u00ed country, the bells said, Come in,  \\nand Jesuits built a town where the forest had been.  \\nNot a fortress exactly, not heaven on lease\\u2014  \\na reducci\\u00f3n: shared fields, a plaza, some peace.\\n\\nThey taught the children hymns, and the elders the trade;  \\ncarvers shaped saints from the cedar shade.  \\nOn Sunday, the choir rose clear as a river,  \\nthen drums made the whole town fiesta together.\\n\\n\\u201cIs this Rome?\\u201d someone asked. \\u201cNo, friend\\u2014  \\nit\\u2019s the mission, where the furrows bend.\\u201d  \\nThey planted maize, translated prayer,  \\nand argued with governors who wanted their share.\\n\\nFor a while, the bells and the harvest agreed;  \\nthen crowns drew borders, and soldiers took heed.  \\nThe Jesuits left; the settlements frayed,  \\nand history called it progress, then looked away.\\n\\nStill, in the stonework, the old voices persist:  \\na hymn in the dust, a name on a list.  \\nAnd somewhere a village, remembering the cost,  \\nbeats one more drum for the fiesta they lost.\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:frequency\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-202/memory/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-2871"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:6bd6b4b66c3b94eacd332b8b093890b3ff87a6b9e2e3a7e7dd157bb6bd88241b", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2957", "family": "ifeval-source-2957", "sample_id": "sha256:1ab57adc84d9c4b3c99e84d49b7d4cdc5c17dd79655245f17175896dcf6a90ee", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Rewrite the limerick in a strange way. In particular, the limerick is about nursery and storytelling. But do not mention nursery and storytelling in your entire response.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"Please paste the limerick you\\u2019d like me to rewrite.\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:forbidden_words\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-202/memory/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-2957"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:8587bad5fa667bcff56fc745d8638ae7c64aad2503990f6cc75b91d5ab3d494b", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1051", "family": "ifeval-source-1051", "sample_id": "sha256:69c58d2f81c1b58fd56f522f9370df4ce4bf73b367d2b195155aadd9058654c9", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": false, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a letter to a friend in all lowercase letters ask them to go and vote.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"dear friend,\\n\\nplease go and vote. your voice matters, and every vote helps shape our community and future.\\n\\nwith care,\\n\\n[Your Name]\", \"checks\": {\"0:change_case:english_lowercase\": false}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-202/memory/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-1051"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "failure", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:95c01de16d483582ee8b5958a75254b3d42f8162b62764b5ffea42cc06d6d599", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1531", "family": "ifeval-source-1531", "sample_id": "sha256:115e1d8ef7a0ee1a4008851dd38f6a963b6641b7a8c1adb76478fc068dd24079", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Come up with a proposal for a new research project on how to improve the quality of life for people with disabilities. Your response should be able to be rendered as HTML, and should include the keywords 'atlantis' and 'constable'.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"<article>\\n  <h1>Inclusive Futures: A Research Project to Improve Quality of Life for People with Disabilities</h1>\\n\\n  <section>\\n    <h2>Project Summary</h2>\\n    <p>\\n      <strong>Inclusive Futures</strong> will investigate how accessible technology, inclusive public services,\\n      and community-based support can improve independence, health, employment, and social participation for\\n      people with disabilities. The project will be designed and evaluated with disabled people as co-researchers,\\n      ensuring that outcomes reflect lived experience rather than assumptions.\\n    </p>\\n  </section>\\n\\n  <section>\\n    <h2>Research Questions</h2>\\n    <ul>\\n      <li>Which environmental, technological, and social barriers most strongly reduce quality of life?</li>\\n      <li>Which combinations of assistive technology, transportation, healthcare, and employment support produce the greatest benefits?</li>\\n      <li>How can services be made more affordable, culturally responsive, and accessible?</li>\\n      <li>How do outcomes differ across physical, sensory, intellectual, and psychosocial disabilities?</li>\\n    </ul>\\n  </section>\\n\\n  <section>\\n    <h2>Methods</h2>\\n    <ol>\\n      <li><strong>Participatory design:</strong> Establish an advisory council led by people with diverse disabilities.</li>\\n      <li><strong>Baseline study:</strong> Collect surveys, interviews, mobility data, and service-access information from participating communities.</li>\\n      <li><strong>Community pilots:</strong> Test interventions such as accessible digital navigation tools, peer-support networks, flexible employment pathways, and coordinated care.</li>\\n      <li><strong>Evaluation:</strong> Compare changes in wellbeing, autonomy, social connection, employment, healthcare access, and financial security over 12\\u201324 months.</li>\\n      <li><strong>Implementation research:</strong> Identify the policies, costs, training, and partnerships needed to scale successful interventions.</li>\\n    </ol>\\n  </section>\\n\\n  <section>\\n    <h2>Innovation</h2>\\n    <p>\\n      The project will create an open-access \\u201cQuality of Life Accessibility Index\\u201d that combines objective\\n      measures with participant-defined priorities. A fictional pilot community, <em>Atlantis</em>, may be used\\n      as a neutral test case for simulation and service planning, while the implementation framework will be\\n      called the <em>Constable model</em>: co-designed, observable, networked, sustainable, transparent,\\n      accessible, and locally led.\\n    </p>\\n  </section>\\n\\n  <section>\\n    <h2>Ethics and Inclusion</h2>\\n    <p>\\n      Participants will receive accessible consent materials, fair compensation, privacy protection, and\\n      multiple ways to participate. Researchers will follow disability-led governance principles, avoid\\n      extractive data collection, and report both positive and negative findings.\\n    </p>\\n  </section>\\n\\n  <section>\\n    <h2>Expected Outcomes</h2>\\n    <ul>\\n      <li>Evidence-based recommendations for governments, employers, healthcare providers, and community organizations.</li>\\n      <li>Practical tools for measuring accessibility and quality of life.</li>\\n      <li>Validated interventions that improve independence, belonging, and economic opportunity.</li>\\n      <li>A scalable model for disability-inclusive policy and service delivery.</li>\\n    </ul>\\n  </section>\\n\\n  <section>\\n    <h2>Proposed Timeline and Budget</h2>\\n    <p>\\n      The project will run for three years: six months for co-design and baseline research, 18 months for\\n      community pilots, and 12 months for evaluation and dissemination. Funding should support participant\\n      compensation, accessible research staff, assistive technologies, data security, local partnerships,\\n      and independent evaluation.\\n    </p>\\n  </section>\\n\\n  <section>\\n    <h2>Success Criteria</h2>\\n    <p>\\n      Success will be defined by measurable improvements in participant-reported wellbeing and autonomy,\\n      reduced barriers to essential services, increased participation in education or employment, and the\\n      sustained adoption of project recommendations by partner organizations.\\n    </p>\\n  </section>\\n</article>\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:existence\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-202/memory/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-1531"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:d52bd6985d5e21d69bfd115dfa37181be16836c33489562824e6aaf6c8065ba6", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1759", "family": "ifeval-source-1759", "sample_id": "sha256:d9e6ea16072179403b2815f0385ecd27e032c6a329b6c4c148be3e13f7af1714", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "How to write a good Chinese poem? At the end of your response, please explicitly add a note starting with \"P.S.\"", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"To write a good Chinese poem:\\n\\n1. **Begin with a clear image or emotion**  \\n   Start from something concrete\\u2014rain on a window, a farewell, autumn leaves\\u2014rather than an abstract idea.\\n\\n2. **Use concise, vivid language**  \\n   Chinese poetry values economy. Choose strong nouns and verbs; remove unnecessary words.\\n\\n3. **Create rhythm and sound**  \\n   Pay attention to line length, pauses, repetition, and\\u2014especially in classical poetry\\u2014rhyme and tonal patterns.\\n\\n4. **Show emotion indirectly**  \\n   Let images suggest feelings. \\u201c\\u5b64\\u706f\\u7167\\u65e7\\u8863\\u201d may express loneliness more powerfully than \\u201c\\u6211\\u5f88\\u5b64\\u72ec.\\u201d\\n\\n5. **Build contrast and movement**  \\n   Pair stillness with motion, light with darkness, past with present, or distance with intimacy.\\n\\n6. **Use culturally resonant imagery carefully**  \\n   Moonlight, rivers, plum blossoms, and autumn wind can be powerful, but give familiar images a fresh context.\\n\\n7. **Revise aloud**  \\n   Read the poem repeatedly. Replace awkward sounds, cut clich\\u00e9s, and ensure every line contributes something.\\n\\nA useful structure is:\\n\\n> **\\u666f\\uff08scene\\uff09 \\u2192 \\u60c5\\uff08emotion\\uff09 \\u2192 \\u8f6c\\uff08shift or insight\\uff09 \\u2192 \\u610f\\uff08afterthought or resonance\\uff09**\\n\\nFor example:\\n\\n> \\u96e8\\u843d\\u7a7a\\u9636\\u665a\\uff0c  \\n> \\u706f\\u660e\\u534a\\u5377\\u4e66\\u3002  \\n> \\u6b32\\u5bfb\\u5f52\\u53bb\\u8def\\uff0c  \\n> \\u4e91\\u5728\\u6545\\u5c71\\u5c45\\u3002\\n\\nP.S. A good Chinese poem does not need to sound ancient; clarity, memorable images, and genuine feeling matter most.\", \"checks\": {\"0:detectable_content:postscript\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-202/memory/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-1759"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}], "memory": [{"mode_id": "lowercase_constraint_signature_exception", "description": "A response-wide lowercase constraint is violated by a mixed-case signature placeholder: the letter body is lowercase, but \u201c[Your Name]\u201d contains capitals. The supplied data contains only one failure of this mechanism, so recurrence is not established; no success shares its family, environment, and policy.", "support_case_ids": ["sha256:cb3e36d1d14b724f2c27ae7a7f952b79400e9237e26a16a2dbc3d40a1acee404"], "counterexample_case_ids": [], "families": ["ifeval-source-1051"], "diagnoser_id": "sha256:8753df9d317681692bd865abf2336f8ec5139b83c55512df2bc6f1bd4d9c59b5", "state": "active", "mastery": {"mode_id": "lowercase_constraint_signature_exception", "mastered": false, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-1051"], "schema_version": 1}, "schema_version": 1}]}

