5\\u65f6\\u95f4\\u91cd\\u8bfb\\uff0c\\u5220\\u6389\\u89e3\\u91ca\\u6027\\u53e5\\u5b50\\uff0c\\u8c03\\u6574\\u987a\\u5e8f\\uff0c\\u5e76\\u5927\\u58f0\\u6717\\u8bf5\\u68c0\\u9a8c\\u8282\\u594f\\u3002\\n\\n\\u4e00\\u4e2a\\u7b80\\u5355\\u7684\\u5199\\u4f5c\\u6b65\\u9aa4\\u662f\\uff1a**\\u786e\\u5b9a\\u60c5\\u611f \\u2192 \\u9009\\u62e9\\u610f\\u8c61 \\u2192 \\u5199\\u51fa\\u521d\\u7a3f \\u2192 \\u5220\\u9664\\u5957\\u8bdd \\u2192 \\u8c03\\u6574\\u8282\\u594f \\u2192 \\u7559\\u4e0b\\u4f59\\u97f5**\\u3002\\n\\n**P.S.** \\u597d\\u8bd7\\u4e0d\\u4e00\\u5b9a\\u534e\\u4e3d\\uff0c\\u4f46\\u4e00\\u5b9a\\u771f\\u8bda\\u3001\\u5177\\u4f53\\uff0c\\u5e76\\u4e14\\u6709\\u5c5e\\u4e8e\\u81ea\\u5df1\\u7684\\u58f0\\u97f3\\u3002\", \"checks\": {\"0:detectable_content:postscript\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-1759"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:66851f7fd7a1fa9f8d0c5717528548706a406746fb2015ae7bc1fa354cd43003", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1675", "family": "ifeval-source-1675", "sample_id": "sha256:a55a699a19a132f9b6746f1ae57d0e610a0eea3771dc114b87e389726936e003", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Can you provide a translation for \"\u4eca\u5929\u5929\u6c14\u5f88\u597d\" in German? Do not use \"heute\". Please use another word.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"Das Wetter ist am heutigen Tag sehr sch\\u00f6n.\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:forbidden_words\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-1675"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:6af22dd758937ff3a30cfe5ab2873e78c32c1cd38a296f60bd82e314e26dd116", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2871", "family": "ifeval-source-2871", "sample_id": "sha256:03a2df55774cdee07d56a8ff8b8c07fb38953cc310374e8bd86b5b62420aecd0", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a poem about the history of reductions in the context of the church. Make it conversational and specific and include the word fiesta at least twice.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"In 1609, a Jesuit said,  \\n\\u201cCome in from the forest\\u2014we\\u2019ll build a town,\\u201d  \\nand the Guaran\\u00ed answered carefully,  \\nbringing maize, songs, and the names of their dead.\\n\\nThey called it a reduction,  \\nnot because anyone felt reduced,  \\nbut because scattered families  \\nwere gathered into one church bell\\u2019s reach.\\n\\nIn Paraguay, the plaza filled at dusk:  \\nmen learning hymns, women trading woven cloth,  \\nchildren racing past the workshops  \\nwhile a priest argued over the price of salt.\\n\\nOn feast days, the whole town became a fiesta\\u2014  \\ndrums under the chapel eaves,  \\nred peppers, bright feathers,  \\nand a Mass that lasted until the shadows cooled.\\n\\nStill, \\u201cshelter\\u201d came with rules.  \\nThe missions taught farming, music, and letters,  \\nbut guarded old customs with suspicion,  \\nand Spain\\u2019s officials counted people like coins.\\n\\nThen soldiers arrived in 1756,  \\nmaps folded in their pockets,  \\nand the reductions were told to move\\u2014  \\nas if a village could simply pick up its bell.\\n\\nSome resisted; some fled.  \\nThe great churches emptied slowly,  \\ntheir painted saints watching vines  \\nclimb over the doors.\\n\\nToday, ruins stand where the fiesta once rose:  \\nstone walls, broken arches,  \\na quiet field where someone still imagines  \\nthe choir beginning again.\\n\\nHistory rarely says, \\u201cI was complicated.\\u201d  \\nIt says mission, conversion, progress\\u2014  \\nthen leaves us to ask who spoke,  \\nwho stayed, and who paid for the music.\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:frequency\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-2871"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:a95306c482dea8bb4a5ecddd8504c41700fa3f7bb9437e0c31f4fd1754c2482c", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1531", "family": "ifeval-source-1531", "sample_id": "sha256:745f7c7d731e1187a0542a061744e6498f7566013c4624cb25ac06b719c6c88b", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Come up with a proposal for a new research project on how to improve the quality of life for people with disabilities. Your response should be able to be rendered as HTML, and should include the keywords 'atlantis' and 'constable'.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"<!DOCTYPE html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n  <meta charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\">\\n  <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\\\">\\n  <title>Inclusive Living Lab Research Proposal</title>\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n  <article>\\n    <h1>Inclusive Living Lab</h1>\\n    <h2>A Research Project to Improve Quality of Life for People with Disabilities</h2>\\n\\n    <h3>Executive Summary</h3>\\n    <p>\\n      The Inclusive Living Lab will investigate how accessible technology, community services,\\n      and person-centered policy can work together to improve independence, wellbeing, and\\n      social participation for people with disabilities. The project will be designed and\\n      evaluated with disabled people as research partners, not merely as study participants.\\n    </p>\\n\\n    <h3>Research Questions</h3>\\n    <ol>\\n      <li>Which combinations of assistive technology and local services produce the greatest improvements in daily autonomy?</li>\\n      <li>How can public spaces, transportation, healthcare, and employment systems become more accessible and coordinated?</li>\\n      <li>What measures best capture quality of life across different disabilities, ages, cultures, and socioeconomic backgrounds?</li>\\n      <li>How can innovations remain affordable, privacy-preserving, adaptable, and sustainable?</li>\\n    </ol>\\n\\n    <h3>Project Design</h3>\\n    <p>\\n      The project will take place over three years in several diverse communities. A disability-led\\n      advisory board will guide priorities, recruitment, consent procedures, accessibility standards,\\n      and interpretation of results.\\n    </p>\\n\\n    <h4>Work Package 1: Needs and Barriers Assessment</h4>\\n    <p>\\n      Researchers will conduct interviews, participatory workshops, accessibility audits, and\\n      surveys to identify barriers in housing, transportation, education, work, healthcare, and\\n      social life.\\n    </p>\\n\\n    <h4>Work Package 2: Co-Design and Prototyping</h4>\\n    <p>\\n      Mixed teams of disabled residents, caregivers, designers, clinicians, engineers, and service\\n      providers will develop practical interventions. Potential interventions include navigation\\n      tools, adaptive-home features, coordinated service plans, accessible communication systems,\\n      and peer-support networks.\\n    </p>\\n\\n    <h4>Work Package 3: Community Pilot</h4>\\n    <p>\\n      Selected interventions will be tested in real-world settings using an inclusive evaluation\\n      framework. Participants will be able to customize or decline any technology, and non-digital\\n      alternatives will always be available.\\n    </p>\\n\\n    <h4>Work Package 4: Evaluation and Scale-Up</h4>\\n    <p>\\n      Outcomes will be compared before and after implementation, with attention to differences\\n      across disability type, gender, age, race, income, and geographic location. The project will\\n      produce implementation guides for municipalities, employers, healthcare organizations, and\\n      community groups.\\n    </p>\\n\\n    <h3>Evaluation Measures</h3>\\n    <ul>\\n      <li>Self-reported wellbeing, autonomy, and life satisfaction</li>\\n      <li>Participation in education, employment, healthcare, and community activities</li>\\n      <li>Time, cost, and effort required to access essential services</li>\\n      <li>Loneliness, social connection, and caregiver burden</li>\\n      <li>Accessibility, usability, privacy, and affordability of each intervention</li>\\n    </ul>\\n\\n    <h3>Ethics and Inclusion</h3>\\n    <p>\\n      The study will use accessible consent materials, compensated participation, flexible\\n      scheduling, sign-language interpretation, captioning, screen-reader-compatible documents,\\n      and trauma-informed procedures. Data governance will be transparent, with participants\\n      retaining meaningful control over how their information is collected and used.\\n    </p>\\n\\n    <h3>Expected Outcomes</h3>\\n    <p>\\n      The project will deliver evidence-based recommendations, open accessibility standards,\\n      tested community interventions, and a replicable model for disability-led research. It will\\n      also identify which solutions improve quality of life without increasing surveillance,\\n      exclusion, or financial burden.\\n    </p>\\n\\n    <h3>Distinctive Contribution</h3>\\n    <p>\\n      Rather than treating accessibility as a single product or infrastructure problem, the\\n      Inclusive Living Lab will study the entire ecosystem surrounding daily life. The project\\n      will use the exploratory concept name <strong>Atlantis</strong> for its integrated data and\\n      service-mapping platform, while <strong>Constable</strong> will designate the independent\\n      ethics and participant-safety review process.\\n    </p>\\n\\n    <h3>Conclusion</h3>\\n    <p>\\n      Improving quality of life requires solutions shaped by the people who will use them.\\n      By combining disability leadership, community co-design, rigorous evaluation, and responsible\\n      innovation, this project can generate practical improvements while establishing a stronger\\n      foundation for inclusive public policy.\\n    </p>\\n  </article>\\n</body>\\n</html>\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:existence\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-1531"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:ba438d77206ef38290809e733e519932b9273968f4affa98946fd9960082a32d", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2265", "family": "ifeval-source-2265", "sample_id": "sha256:575dde2414f7f56df5c5c6b51a069c6f94aba9a058779ff198b09027bef84318", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a freestyle rap about the president of the united states. The letter q should show up at least 4 times.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"President in the spotlight, stepping to the mic,  \\nQuarterback of the nation, making choices we like.  \\nQuick with the questions, questing for the truth,  \\nQuaking up the system, bringing fresh proof.  \\n\\nFrom the Capitol steps to the people in the queue,  \\nQuiet hopes rise up in a red, white, blue view.  \\nQ on the rhythm, every line coming through\\u2014  \\nLeading with a vision, making history new.\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:letter_frequency\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-2265"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:c0d4aa88ce3011e5d172ce8db2633782800c712c0e9f35a6f81dded397572cf1", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1999", "family": "ifeval-source-1999", "sample_id": "sha256:7b2a3d564aa1339dbe97e62a03069dda88a47e0722dbda6fb415e5f040ae0d39", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Generate a summary of the following passage in all capital letters:\n\nWorld War II or the Second World War, often abbreviated as WWII or WW2, was a global conflict that lasted from 1939 to 1945. The vast majority of the world's countries, including all of the great powers, fought as part of two opposing military alliances: the Allies and the Axis. Many participants threw their economic, industrial, and scientific capabilities behind this total war, blurring the distinction between civilian and military resources. Aircraft played a major role, enabling the strategic bombing of population centres and the delivery of the only two nuclear weapons ever used in war. World War II was by far the deadliest conflict in history, resulting in an estimated 70 to 85 million fatalities, mostly among civilians. Tens of millions died due to genocides (including the Holocaust), starvation, massacres, and disease. In the wake of Axis defeat, Germany, Austria and Japan were occupied, and war crimes tribunals were conducted against German and Japanese leaders.\n\n", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"WORLD WAR II WAS A GLOBAL CONFLICT FROM 1939 TO 1945, FOUGHT BETWEEN THE ALLIES AND AXIS. IT INVOLVED TOTAL WAR, STRATEGIC BOMBING, AND THE USE OF NUCLEAR WEAPONS. IT WAS HISTORY\\u2019S DEADLIEST WAR, CAUSING 70\\u201385 MILLION DEATHS, INCLUDING VICTIMS OF GENOCIDE, STARVATION, MASSACRES, AND DISEASE. AFTER THE AXIS DEFEAT, OCCUPATIONS AND WAR CRIMES TRIALS FOLLOWED.\", \"checks\": {\"0:change_case:english_capital\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-1999"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:cb3e36d1d14b724f2c27ae7a7f952b79400e9237e26a16a2dbc3d40a1acee404", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1051", "family": "ifeval-source-1051", "sample_id": "sha256:0a9860f30f3adad60e7c750b3204e779da8756baf97348a799c9b4bc8aa30c88", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": false, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a letter to a friend in all lowercase letters ask them to go and vote.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"dear friend,\\n\\ni hope you\\u2019re doing well. i wanted to remind you to go and vote. your voice matters, and every vote helps shape our community and future. please make a plan to participate if you can.\\n\\nwith care,\\n\\n[Your Name]\", \"checks\": {\"0:change_case:english_lowercase\": false}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-1051"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "failure", "schema_version": 1}], "memory": []}

